    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** stands as our highest-upside play with a robust 70.47 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Bieber (xERA 5.10) combined with a high-leverage spot in the 2-hole provides a premium floor for run production. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a staple in our lineup; while he faces a tougher arm in Bradley, his capacity to exploit base-stealing opportunities against a slower-to-the-plate pitcher keeps his score firmly in the \"Strong\" territory at 65.73. We are also monitoring **Geraldo Perdomo**, who gets a solid boost to 58.07 due to his elevated batting order position, helping stabilize our categories despite a mediocre matchup against McGreevy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involved **Gavin Sheets**, who fell just short of our 40-point threshold with a score of 35.12. Despite his raw power, the optimizer correctly flagged the aggressive penalty for facing an elite southpaw like Sale (xERA 3.14), which neutered his platoon advantage and forced him into a reserve role to preserve our limited game caps. Meanwhile, **Masyn Winn** (53.61) and **Gleyber Torres** (59.17) provide necessary stability in the middle infield, though **Gleyber Torres** bears watching; his platoon split against right-handed pitching created a significant drag on his ceiling, making his performance vital to our HR and RBI output today. With **Will Smith** confirmed on the IL and **Cal Raleigh** and **Bryce Harper** enjoying scheduled off-days, we are leaning heavily on our active core to avoid any \"Below Floor\" production that could sink our weekly efficiency.",
